{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
  "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Kent E. Cattani",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit's rejection of a reasoned State court factual determination and decision is improper under any deferential standard of review, and it is particularly improper under the highly deferential standard of review required under the AEDPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask about the first one? Does the Constitution require there be no involuntary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In your view, what is the standard for when the district court may hold an evidentiary hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kent E. Cattani",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit clearly held that the State court's determination of the facts was unreasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I mean, is the requirement such that when you ask for a hearing in a State court on a general matter, \"I would like to show through a hearing,\" then he gives a whole lot of affidavits of the kind of thing he's going to produce, that then the State says \"no,\" you go into Federal court and say \"I'm roughly going to do the same thing, I have a few extra witnesses, some of the people say some extra things,\" no, you can't do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. CATTANI)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ineffective assistance --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The criminal gene argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so are you, are you in effect then saying that the waiver does not need to be a knowing waiver in the sense that it needs to be based upon an appreciation of all the possible mitigation evidence that in this case might come in? Are you saying it need not be knowing in that sense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mr. VERRILLI)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DONALD B. VERRILLI, JR. ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "petition for rehearing in which we said, no, you can't rely on that defense because it's got to be a knowing and intelligent waiver under Johnson against Zerbst."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "these witnesses can attest to the use of alcohol and drugs by the biological mother when Landrigan was in utero."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you do it concretely, Mr. Verrilli, for this case. The defendant is being rather obstreperous and says: I don't want any mitigating evidence; I'm a really bad guy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the mental health expert testimony could have been proffered to the Court, had it been prepared and developed, would have been considered, and could have made a critically important difference"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the district court has substantial discretion in determining whether or not to grant that hearing on that basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Ninth Circuit, upon receiving this letter, contacted counsel for Mr. Landrigan, asked him -- asked them to go visit him in prison and find out what's going on. They did so. They reported back to the Ninth Circuit that Mr. Landrigan did in fact want to proceed with the appeals. He has continued to want to proceed with the appeals, signing the IFP papers, et cetera, and it turns out there were neurological problems that were afflicting him, very serious, at the time. So that's what happened."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could say in conclusion, just remind the Court what it said in the first Norrell decision, that even in the world of habeas there's a difference between deference and abdication. And in a situation like this one, in which the State court has not afforded an evidentiary hearing and has not allowed the development of the evidence that bears directly on Mr. Landrigan's claims, it would be a form of abdication to hold that he can be conclusively barred from proceeding further, even to an evidentiary hearing, on the basis of the present record."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1575",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b9a45b3f342a51b447d079636af8645d020bdbe8fe94495b9c2ab8c5ab02b5be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b9a45b3f342a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:55 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
